  "status": "DEPRECATED - CONFIRMED MS41.3 WIDEBAND SPLICE CORRUPTION",
  "tested": false,
  "verification": "Historical MS41.3 V10 is retained only for exact detection, removal and upgrade. Its lambda splice starts inside the SS1v2 wideband-target instructions, changes the calibration pointer and redirects an RPM load into the P3 output latch. Native execution of the failed image reproduces P3 clearing with CUTSW off. Upgrade to MS41.3 V11; this defect does not apply to the separately targeted MS41.0/.1/.2 V10 descriptors.",
  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Adds an independent ignition-cut limiter with its own adjustable RPM hysteresis and fixed injector pulse width while cutting. Launch Control V7 can use the same installed cut engine with separate launch settings and without depending on this limiter's runtime switch.",
  "description": "Ignition Cut V10 with independent standalone and launch requests, hysteresis and fixed IPW. E847.0/.1/.2 are real cut requests; E848.0/.1 track fresh front samples and .2/.3 fresh rear samples where fitted. Active cuts freeze complete trim, mixture and observation transactions. Learning resumes after a native accepted front sample; catalyst observation also requires a fresh rear sample. Native FD30.1 fallback, electrical monitoring, previous misfire/shutdown evidence and completed catalyst results remain effective. No invented recovery timer is used.",
